Fixed. The bug was in `clampToStorageCap` at /Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmpo5vr5wy4/run/src/resources/storage.ts:22 — it clamped wood and stone with `Math.min(resource, cap)` but passed `food` through untouched, so food could be stockpiled without limit. The fix applies the same clamp to food:

```
food: resources.food  →  food: Math.min(resources.food, cap)
```

Verified end-to-end: `advanceTurn` (src/sim/turn.ts:20) runs every turn's production through `clampToStorageCap` with the current storage cap, so food is now capped identically to wood and stone. Also cleaned up the stale "BUG" doc comments that described the old behavior.

Verification: `npm run test` → 15/15 tests pass; `npm run typecheck` → clean.


